{
 "comment": "tds_payees P2-2 at the reference's current head: a bill booked gross with its TDS debited back to the payee (Carrier A, a payee debit equal to the bill's own TDS) is rate-tested on its value before TDS and, deducted at the rate on its own voucher, leaves clause 21(b)(ii)(A) for the question on the payee's TDS; its only listing there still raises the s.194C(6) question on the goods-carriage ledger. A payee debit other than the bill's TDS (Contractor B) makes the bill untested and counted. A later voucher debiting the TDS ledger against the payee (Contractor C) keeps its deducted bill in (ii)(A): the reversal is not judged. A cash-paid bill carrying TDS (no payee named) is counted as untested.",
